  {"comment": "The three gores of a 90-degree elbow of centre-line radius 60 (two joints, each cut at 22.5 degrees, tan a = 0.41421356), made each as its own body on the Y axis: a tube revolved about Y, cut by planes through Z. The middle gore (F3) runs from y = -x tan a to y = Lm + x tan a, Lm = 120 tan a = 49.7056: its generator at x = 19.5 cos(s / 19.5) along the neutral surface is Lm + 2 (19.5 tan a) cos(s / 19.5) long, the heel (x = 19.5, where the revolve's seam is) 65.8600, the throat 33.5513. Opened at the seam by the corner gap (the thickness, 1): the blank is Lm (39 pi - 1) - 4 19.5^2 tan a sin(1 / 39) = 6024.1803, and with K 0.5 the sheet holds it times the thickness. The cut ends are not normal to the material: a warning."},
